## --- Old Man Holstenoffer (`story.ni:4538-4577`) ---------------------------

create Old Man Holstenoffer
  aka holstenoffer, old man, butcher, the butcher, proprietor, shopkeeper, shop keeper, merchant
  a person, proper
  pronouns he
  in the Butcher's Shop
  carries the cleaver

  Holstenoffer is a squat brick of a man, with a scarred bulldog's face and
  sailors' tattoos covering his arms from the wrists all the way up to his
  rolled-up sleeves. He's friendly enough and loves to gossip, but he has a
  tendency to gesticulate with his cleaver in hand, which sometimes makes
  conversation with him a tense and athletic affair.

  on every turn while Old Man Holstenoffer is here and one chance in 5
    phrase holstenoffer-idle
  end on

  on the player talking
    refuse holstenoffer-ho1-stub
  end on

create the cleaver
  aka big molly, molly, knife, holstenoffer's cleaver, bloody cleaver

  Holstenoffer calls his cleaver 'Big Molly,' and often talks to it as though
  it were a pet. The side of the blade is tarnished and dull from years of use,
  but the edge is sharp enough to hack through thick muscle and bone like they
  were pudding.

create the tattoos
  aka tattoo, sailors' tattoos, blue tangle, swirling designs, designs, arms
  scenery, plural
  in the Butcher's Shop

  Holstenoffer's tattoos are a solid blue tangle of swirling designs, covering
  his arms from his wrists all the way up to his rolled-up sleeves.

## `ATMOS_Holstenoffer` (`story.ni:4560`) — the source's one dramatic event
## here, carried as plain every-turn texture (P-9: the port ships without
## deferred narration).

define phrase holstenoffer-idle, randomly
  Holstenoffer's cleaver cuts through a particularly tough joint with a
  gristly, crunching sound.
or
  Holstenoffer chops deftly at the raw meat on his block, cutting into narrow
  strips.
or
  Holstenoffer stops to wipe his hands on his blood-smeared apron.
or
  Holstenoffer stops suddenly and holds up a slippery-looking chunk of red
  gristle. 'Huh,' he mutters, 'never seen one of those before.' With a shrug,
  he tosses it into a tray labeled 'Bargain Bits.'
end phrase

