## --- Olgan Minor (`story.ni:4736-4762`) ------------------------------------
## The talent sentence prints on the first examine only (an ordinal block in
## the examine reaction), as the source's `[first time]` does.

create Olgan Minor
  aka minor, olgan, proprietor, shopkeeper, shop keeper, merchant, man, armorer
  a person, proper
  pronouns he
  in the Armory

  Olgan Minor is short but muscular, with a lined face and graying,
  military-cut hair. He says nothing as you browse his wares, but his eyes seem
  to bore right into you.

  after the player examining
    first time
      phrase minor-talent
  end after

  on every turn while Olgan Minor is here and one chance in 5
    phrase minor-idle
  end on

  on the player talking
    refuse minor-om1-stub
  end on

define phrase minor-talent
  You are suddenly certain that he knows you're not really a boy — that he
  knew it the instant you walked into his shop.
end phrase

define phrase minor-idle, randomly
  Minor's eyes seem to drill right into you.
or
  Minor trims his nails with a small knife. The whole time, he never stops
  staring at you. He never blinks.
or
  Olgan Minor's constant staring is really starting to creep you out. You
  find yourself wishing you'd never entered his shop.
end phrase

## `OM1` opens on `talk to` (`story.ni:4763`). Olgan HAS the talent (change
## document, "Who sees her"): the first perceiver in the game who is hostile.

define phrase minor-om1-stub
  (TODO during play-testing — conversation OM1: "'Um, mind if I ask you
  something?'" — Olgan's tree, 8 first-visit quips; Olgan Minor SEES her, and
  says so in his own way.)
